# React + TypeScript

Applies when working under `frontend/`.

## MUST

- Functional components. TypeScript strict; no `any` as a shortcut.
- Tailwind-compatible styling. Do not add a second CSS framework.
- Typed API client + typed WebSocket client matching backend contracts (`data-contract-review`).
- Timeline: Recharts (area/line, sentiment polarity, time-window control).
- Network: `react-force-graph-2d` (nodes/links, PageRank-scaled size, community color).
- Demographics: choropleth + profession donut; data from `GET /api/v1/analytics/demographics`.
- Live feed: `event:new_post`; bounded list; malformed events must not crash the UI.
- Analyst filters: topic, time window, severity — dispatch WS criteria, then re-render from backend data.
- Loading, empty, and error states on every widget.
- Wire widgets to real REST/WS once those exist. No disconnected mock dashboards as the product.

## MUST NOT

- Extra global state libraries unless the UI cannot work without them.
- Socket.io client. Use the native WebSocket client against FastAPI.
- Treating optional archive/demo JSON as the primary data path.

```tsx
// BAD
const data: any = await fetch(url).then((r) => r.json());

// GOOD
const data: TimelineResponse = await api.getTimeline(params);
```